<title>MEXICO: Second Mexican labor leader dies.</title>
<headline>Second Mexican labor leader dies.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A second high-level Mexican labor leader, Blas Chumacero Sanchez, died on Saturday of a heart attack, news reports said on Sunday. He was 92.</p>
<p>He was substitute Secretary-general of the six-million strong Mexican Workers Confederation (CTM) and chief of the Worker's Federation of Puebla.</p>
<p>Chumacero died three weeks after the death of long-time union boss Fidel Velazquez Sanchez, who was 97.</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
